      "translatedText": "1. RAII: Bind resource and object lifetimes\\.\n2. `unique_ptr` : Exclusive ownership, the default choice\\.\n3. `shared_ptr` : Use only when multiple owners are genuinely needed\\.\n4. `weak_ptr` : Observe only, do not extend lifetime, used to break reference cycles\\.\n5. Move semantics: Transfer resources out to avoid deep copies of large objects\\.",
